ed by the same shape, coloured to match the small shapes outside. When the program compares a hole with a small shape, it allows rotation and mirroring, so it matches the 8 orientation variants. Several colours can carry the same shape, so the colour that wins is the one with the most copies of that shape.\n\n**Pair 1**\n\n- The 2×2 holes become colour 8: there are five 2×2 squares in colour 8, three in colour 2 and one in colour 3.\n- The plus-shaped hole becomes colour 5: there are two plus shapes in colour 5 and one in colour 6.\n- The 1×2 dominoes become colour 9. They are vertical in some places and horizontal in others, and both orientations count as the same shape.\n\n**Pair 2**\n\n- The 3-cell L holes become colour 4: four L shapes in colour 4 against three in colour 2.\n- The single-cell holes become colour 5.\n- The 5-cell corner shapes become colour 3: two in colour 3, one in colour 6.\n- The plus-shaped hole becomes colour 7: colour 7 has more plus shapes than colour 9.\n\n**Construction plan**\n\n1. Crop the bounding box of the largest object. This first canvas shows the holes still unfilled.\n2. Flood every hole in that shape class at once with the winning colour, emitting one stage per hole shape class.\n3. Any cell left over gets the big object's colour.\n\n**Test input**\n\n- The big object is the 4-coloured band in rows 0–6. Its holes are 1-coloured shapes of several kinds.\n- There are many small shapes in colours 2, 3, 6, 7, 8 and 9. Each class of hole shape is looked up the same way, by canonical shape and majority colour.\n- If a hole shape has no matching small shape, the program uses a fallback: it fills the hole with the big object's colour.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    big = max(objs, key=lambda o: o[\"size\"])\n    bc = big[\"colour\"]\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = big[\"box\"]\n    canvas = crop(g, y0, x0, y1, x1)\n    emit(canvas, \"Crop the bounding box of the large object; its holes still show the background colour.\")\n\n    def canon(cells):\n        arr = np.array(cells)\n        best = None\n        for k in range(8):\n            a = arr.copy()\n            if k & 1: a[:, 0] = -a[:, 0]\n            if k & 2: a[:, 1] = -a[:, 1]\n            if k & 4: a = a[:, ::-1]\n            a = a - a.min(axis=0)\n            t = tuple(sorted(map(tuple, a.tolist())))\n            if best is None or t < best:\n                best = t\n        return best\n\n    # small shapes: shape -> colour counts\n    from collections import Counter, defaultdict\n    table = defaultdict(Counter)\n    for o in objs:\n        if o is big:\n            continue\n        table[canon(o[\"cells\"])][o[\"colour\"]] += 1\n\n    holes = components(canvas != bc)\n    groups = defaultdict(list)\n    for h in holes:\n        groups[canon(h)].append(h)\n\n    out = canvas.copy()\n    for key, hs in groups.items():\n        if key in table and table[key]:\n            col = table[key].most_common(1)[0][0]\n        else:\n            col = bc\n        for h in hs:\n            for (y, x) in h:\n                out[y, x] = col\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Fill all {len(hs)} hole(s) of this shape with colour {col}, the most common colour among loose pieces of that shape.\")\n    out[(out == bg) & (canvas == bg) & False] = bc\n    emit(out, \"Final: every hole replaced by its matching coloured piece.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In it, every hole is replaced by the same shape, coloured to match the small shapes outside."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Several colours can carry the same shape, so the colour that wins is the one with the most copies of that shape."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"They are vertical in some places and horizontal in others, and both orientations count as the same shape."}],"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"When the program compares a hole with a small shape, it allows rotation and mirroring, so it matches the 8 orientation variants."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"That object is pierced by holes in the background colour."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In it, every hole is replaced by the same shape, coloured to match the small shapes outside."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"When the program compares a hole with a small shape, it allows rotation and mirroring, so it matches the 8 orientation variants."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"They are vertical in some places and horizontal in others, and both orientations count as the same shape."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The output is the large object's bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Crop the bounding box of the largest object."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Crop the bounding box of the large object; its holes still show the background colour."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"11ee47d14e95bb2cc0cb27c869d53fb398c050774baed0da1ba00b79497d1ec7","task_sha256":"e9ec3118c6d0c60d5325e0057aec77b5456b371cac034a00ad41e0d416b5191c","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
